steps.message:
You ruled out a DI container and cannot change the released public static signatures, so use an internal ambient clock backed by `AsyncLocal<T>`. Expose the internal override only to the test assembly with `InternalsVisibleTo`; the public API remains unchanged.

```csharp
using System.Runtime.CompilerServices;
using System.Threading;

[assembly: InternalsVisibleTo("Contoso.Retention.Tests")]

public static class RetentionPolicy
{
    private static readonly AsyncLocal<Func<DateTimeOffset>?> s_clockOverride = new();

    private static DateTimeOffset UtcNow
        => s_clockOverride.Value?.Invoke() ?? TimeProvider.System.GetUtcNow();

    public static bool IsExpired(DateTimeOffset createdAt, TimeSpan retention)
        => UtcNow - createdAt > retention;

    public static DateTimeOffset NextSweep(DateTimeOffset lastSweep)
    {
        var now = UtcNow;
        var scheduled = lastSweep.AddDays(1);
        return scheduled < now ? now : scheduled;
    }

    public static string StampFileName(string prefix)
        => $"{prefix}_{UtcNow.UtcDateTime:yyyyMMddHHmmss}.log";

    internal static IDisposable OverrideClock(TimeProvider provider)
    {
        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(provider);
        var previous = s_clockOverride.Value;
        Func<DateTimeOffset> current = provider.GetUtcNow;
        s_clockOverride.Value = current;
        return new ClockScope(current, previous);
    }

    private sealed class ClockScope(
        Func<DateTimeOffset> current,
        Func<DateTimeOffset>? previous) : IDisposable
    {
        private bool _disposed;

        public void Dispose()
        {
            if (_disposed)
                return;
            if (!ReferenceEquals(s_clockOverride.Value, current))
                throw new InvalidOperationException("Clock scopes must be disposed in LIFO order.");

            s_clockOverride.Value = previous;
            _disposed = true;
        }
    }
}
```

This replaces every `DateTime.UtcNow` read, including both decisions in `NextSweep`, while preserving `DateTimeOffset` and UTC filename semantics. `AsyncLocal` flows across `await`, so parallel tests do not share overrides. The disposable scope restores nested values, ignores duplicate disposal, and rejects out-of-order disposal instead of replaying stale state. Tests can use `FakeTimeProvider`, and only the precisely named friend test assembly can call the internal override. Production still defaults to `TimeProvider.System`; the trade-off is one `AsyncLocal.Value` read per clock access.
